## Interface: 120100
## Title: Ka0s Consumable Master
## Notes: Auto-managed account-wide consumable macros.
## Author: add1kted2ka0s
## Version: 1.6.2
## IconTexture: Interface\AddOns\ConsumableMaster\media\logos\consumablemaster.logo.128.tga
# ConsumableMasterPerfDB is the perf harness's own ring of captures, kept
# separate from the AceDB tree on purpose: LibKa0s-Perf writes the global
# directly, so folding it into ConsumableMasterDB would stamp its keys onto
# AceDB's root and trip AceDB's own discard branch on the next load.
## SavedVariables: ConsumableMasterDB, ConsumableMasterPerfDB
## OptionalDeps: Ace3, LibStub, CallbackHandler-1.0, LibSharedMedia-3.0, LibDataBroker-1.1, LibDBIcon-1.0
## DefaultState: enabled
## Category-enUS: Combat
## X-License: MIT
## X-Standard: https://github.com/tusharsaxena/WowAddonStandards
## X-Curse-Project-ID: 1522944

# Libraries (vendored in libs/ — load first)
libs\LibStub\LibStub.lua
libs\CallbackHandler-1.0\CallbackHandler-1.0.xml
libs\LibSharedMedia-3.0\lib.xml
libs\AceAddon-3.0\AceAddon-3.0.xml
libs\AceEvent-3.0\AceEvent-3.0.xml
libs\AceDB-3.0\AceDB-3.0.xml
# AceDBOptions builds the Profiles page's options table over the AceDB object;
# beside AceDB, as MultiMeters and KickCD place it.
libs\AceDBOptions-3.0\AceDBOptions-3.0.xml
libs\AceConsole-3.0\AceConsole-3.0.xml
libs\AceGUI-3.0\AceGUI-3.0.xml
# AceConfig (Registry, Cmd, Dialog) draws the Profiles page -- its only use in
# this addon (options-ui-§3). AFTER AceGUI, and that is load-bearing:
# AceConfigDialog resolves AceGUI with a non-silent LibStub at file load, so
# ahead of it the file raises unless some other addon happened to load AceGUI
# first. Ace3's own TOC orders the two the same way.
libs\AceConfig-3.0\AceConfig-3.0.xml
# LSM30_Border / LSM30_Font dropdowns (border-style picker on the Macro Bar
# page). Depends on AceGUI + LibSharedMedia, so it loads after both.
libs\AceGUI-3.0-SharedMediaWidgets\widget.xml
# The launcher's two libraries (launcher-§1). LibDataBroker-1.1 first and that
# is load-bearing rather than tidy: LibDBIcon-1.0 resolves it with a NON-silent
# LibStub at file load and calls error() when it answers nil, so the reverse
# order takes the whole addon out. Both sit after CallbackHandler-1.0, which
# LibDBIcon builds its callback registry from, and before LibKa0s: the launcher
# major resolves both with LibStub(..., true) at Register time rather than at
# load, so it would survive the other order -- but nothing is gained by making
# the block depend on that.
libs\LibDataBroker-1.1\LibDataBroker-1.1.lua
libs\LibDBIcon-1.0\LibDBIcon-1.0.lua
# LibKa0s — the Ka0s-owned shared library: fifteen majors, and the file list is
# LibKa0s.xml. Vendored whole-folder from github.com/tusharsaxena/LibKa0s and loaded
# through its own packaged XML, which is the file list. Depends on LibStub
# alone, but it sits last in the block so nothing above it can be reordered
# behind it.
libs\LibKa0s\LibKa0s.xml

# Locales
# Position within this group is conventional, not load-bearing.
locales\enUS.lua

# Core
# Namespace.lua first: names the private addon table (`local addonName, NS = ...`)
# and the version string PerfSetup reads at load.
# ConsumableMaster.lua promotes NS to the AceAddon object and owns the DB
# bootstrap + recompute pipeline. Constants (KCM.PREFIX), CoreSetup (KCM.Say off
# LibKa0s-Core-1.0), Compat (spec, spell and item API seam), State (session-only flags),
# and Database (SV migrations) load next; the pure engine modules
# (SpecHelper → Classifier) follow.
core\Namespace.lua
# LifecycleSetup builds the ONE latch (LibKa0s-Lifecycle-1.0) the disabled state
# and the perf harness's suspended arm are two named holds on (slash-commands-§7).
# It sits HERE, and the position is load-bearing: core/PerfSetup.lua below builds
# its probe with `lifecycle = KCM.Lifecycle`, which Perf.lua minor 12 requires, so
# the instance has to exist first. Everything it reaches outward through -- the
# bus, KCM:OnEnable's list, the macro bar, the printer -- is a call-time thunk.
core\LifecycleSetup.lua
# PerfSetup builds the A/B capture harness from LibKa0s-Perf-1.0. Both sides of
# its position are load-bearing. performance-§1 requires it BEFORE any file that
# takes `local Perf = NS.Perf` as a load-time upvalue -- core\ConsumableMaster.lua
# and modules\MacroBar.lua both do. And it must come AFTER core\LifecycleSetup.lua,
# because it reads two things at load: KCM.VERSION (hence that constant lives in
# core\Namespace.lua) and the KCM.Lifecycle instance it passes as
# descriptor.lifecycle, without which it returns before building the probe. The
# run log, the printer, the `perf` hold itself and the macro bar are all reached
# through thunks at call time, so loading before them costs nothing.
core\PerfSetup.lua
# MediaSetup publishes the LibKa0s-Media-1.0 seam (KCM.Icon / KCM.MediaFont) and
# makes the one LibSharedMedia registration for the shipped face. THE POSITION IS
# LOAD-BEARING: core\DebugLogSetup.lua resolves the console's font path EAGERLY at
# load (lib:New type-checks the field and raises), so a MediaSetup that loaded
# after it would resolve that path to nil. Before every consumer, therefore, and
# not merely conventionally early.
core\MediaSetup.lua
core\ConsumableMaster.lua
core\Bus.lua
core\Constants.lua
# CoreSetup builds KCM.Say / KCM.SafeToString from LibKa0s-Core-1.0. It has to
# sit after Constants.lua (KCM.PREFIX) and before core\SlashCommands.lua, which
# takes the printer as a file-scope upvalue.
core\CoreSetup.lua
core\Compat.lua
# EnvSetup reads this addon's own TOC manifest through LibKa0s-Env-1.0 (the
# `/cm version` banner and the About page's notes). Position is conventional --
# nothing here resolves at load beyond the LibStub lookup, and both callers live
# in settings/, which loads later.
core\EnvSetup.lua
# The LibKa0s-Item-1.0 seam. Anywhere after the libs block and before
# settings\Category.lua, which is its only caller.
core\ItemSetup.lua
# LauncherSetup builds the minimap button and the broker plugin from
# LibKa0s-Launcher-1.0 as ONE object (launcher-§1). Position is
# conventional -- it resolves the library at load and nothing else: the db,
# KCM.Options.Open, KCM.Say and the macro bar's lock seam are all reached
# through thunks at Register time, and Register itself runs from
# KCM:OnInitialize, after AceDB has built db.global.minimap.
core\LauncherSetup.lua
core\State.lua
# DebugLogSetup builds the on-screen console from LibKa0s-DebugLog-1.0
# (debug-logging-§1 names the file and the folder). It sits after
# core\Constants.lua + core\CoreSetup.lua (the printer it thunks onto) and
# core\State.lua (KCM.State.debug, the flag's single home), and before
# core\Debug.lua and every other file that writes to the sink. Every seam it
# reaches outward through -- the printer, KCM.State, KCM.Options.Refresh -- is a
# call-time thunk, so nothing here is a load-time dependency.
core\DebugLogSetup.lua
core\Database.lua
core\Debug.lua
core\SpecHelper.lua
core\TooltipCache.lua
core\WeaponSlots.lua
core\BagScanner.lua
core\Classifier.lua
# MacroDisplay reads what a macro currently resolves to (icon/count/cooldown/
# tooltip); MacroBarModel + MacroBarLayout are the pure slot-order and grid-math
# halves of the optional macro bar rendered by modules\MacroBar.lua.
core\MacroDisplay.lua
core\MacroBarModel.lua
core\MacroBarLayout.lua
# SlashDump before SlashCommands: the `/cm dump` targets are a leaf that only
# reads addon state, and SlashCommands' `priority` verb renders composite
# categories through the `pick` target. The dispatcher that binds both is
# settings\Slash.lua (CM-47).
core\SlashDump.lua
core\SlashCommands.lua

# Defaults
# Profile.lua first: KCM.dbDefaults, the AceDB defaults tree and THE
# declaration site for every shipped default (savedvariables-§2). It sits at
# the head of this block so it is evaluated in the same position it held when
# it lived at the top of core/ConsumableMaster.lua — after the whole # Core
# block, before defaults/Categories.lua, which its `perRow` comment relies on.
defaults\Profile.lua
defaults\Categories.lua
defaults\Defaults_StatPriority.lua
defaults\Defaults_Food.lua
defaults\Defaults_Drink.lua
defaults\Defaults_StatFood.lua
defaults\Defaults_HPPot.lua
defaults\Defaults_MPPot.lua
defaults\Defaults_Healthstone.lua
defaults\Defaults_CombatPot.lua
defaults\Defaults_Flask.lua
defaults\Defaults_Vantus.lua
defaults\Defaults_WpnEnch.lua
defaults\Defaults_AugRune.lua
defaults\Defaults_Bloodlust.lua
defaults\Defaults_BattleRez.lua

# Modules
# Position within this group is conventional, not load-bearing.
modules\Ranker.lua
modules\Selector.lua
modules\MacroManager.lua
modules\MacroBarFlyout.lua
modules\MacroBarButton.lua
modules\MacroBar.lua
modules\KCMIconButton.lua
modules\KCMScoreButton.lua
modules\KCMMacroDragIcon.lua
modules\KCMItemRow.lua

# Settings
# settings/SchemaStub.lua -- the LibKa0s-Schema-1.0 degradation stub (KCM.SchemaStub),
# the write seam settings/Panel.lua builds when the library is absent. It only
# has to precede Panel.lua, which takes it at file load; nothing else reads it.
settings\SchemaStub.lua
# settings/OptionsSetup.lua next: it is the LibKa0s-Options-1.0 seam (the panel
# chrome and the scroll container) and the only place the library is
# constructed. It creates KCM.Settings.Helpers and publishes the instance as
# KCM.Settings.optionsUI, which settings/Panel.lua takes as a file-scope local —
# so it has to load before Panel.lua, not after.
settings\OptionsSetup.lua
# settings/Panel.lua next: the addon's own half — the schema rows, the
# LibKa0s-Schema-1.0 write seam and its Get/Set/FindSchema/ValidateSchema
# helpers, the SetAndRefresh door, the wrappers that shadow a library member — and it exposes
# KCM.Settings.RegisterTab, which the per-tab modules below call.
# It also publishes the KCM.Options shim (Register/Refresh/RequestRefresh/Open)
# so the core / pipeline callers keep working unchanged.
settings\Panel.lua
# settings/OptionsShim.lua — the RUN-time half of the same shim: O.Refresh,
# O.RequestRefresh, O.Open, the refresh debounce behind them and the three bus
# subscriptions that drive them. Peeled off Panel.lua at the 1500-line cap
# (layout-§1). Immediately after Panel.lua and that is load-bearing in one
# direction only: it takes KCM.Settings.Helpers, the optionsUI instance and
# Panel.lua's panel-unavailable notice as file-scope locals, so it cannot load
# before them. Nothing below reads it at load -- the page files reach
# KCM.Options through call-time thunks -- so its only constraint is to come
# after Panel.lua.
settings\OptionsShim.lua
# The four page files: position within this group is conventional, not load-bearing.
settings\General.lua
settings\MacroBar.lua
settings\StatPriority.lua
settings\Category.lua
# settings/CategoryAddByID.lua — the Macros page's "Add item or spell by ID"
# line, peeled off Category.lua at the 1500-line cap (layout-§1): the Type
# dropdown, the two ID kinds, this addon's resolver over the library's IdInput
# and O.AddByIDBusy. Immediately AFTER Category.lua and that is load-bearing:
# it takes KCM.Settings.MacrosPage's two helpers as file-scope locals, which
# Category.lua publishes at load. The other direction is call-time only --
# Category.lua reaches KCM.Settings.AddByID.Render while it renders a tab.
settings\CategoryAddByID.lua
# The /cm dispatcher (CM-47). Last in this block because it is the one settings
# file nothing else here reads: it consumes core\SlashCommands.lua's published
# verb table and publishes KCM:OnSlashCommand, which AceConsole resolves by name
# when a command is typed rather than at load.
settings\Slash.lua
# The Profiles page: AceDBOptions' own UI, drawn by AceConfigDialog into this
# addon's canvas. Last, so it is last in the AddOns sidebar -- KCM.Settings.order
# names it last too -- and because nothing loads after it that reads it.
settings\Profiles.lua
